    <Contract id="MESSAGE_LAYOUT">
      A step-boundary / decision message (the decision card) is sectioned with markdown headers, in
      this order. Skip any section empty for this step. During free dialogue inside a step the agent
      does NOT print this layout — it just talks.

      `<dim service line>`        — internal anchor + scope + mode + confidence (supplied by the branch)

      `<breadcrumb>`              — per `BREADCRUMB_FORMAT`, its OWN paragraph (a blank line above it,
      not just a `\n`) — markdown collapses a single newline into a space, so without the blank line
      the breadcrumb visually fuses onto the service line

      ## `<glyph>` `<scope>` — одной фразой, что делаем

      ### 🤔 Как я понял задачу    — an italic blockquote (`> _…_`), 2–3 sentences max: the task retold
      in the agent's own words plus the single riskiest assumption, linked by wording to the question
      that resolves it; never a restate of already-settled content — only what is NEW or could be
      misread (goes at the TOP)
      ### 🎯 Главное решение       — the crux in plain words; if the decision is a flow (data moving,
      state transitions, start/stop conditions), add a small ASCII diagram — the one place a fenced
      block is allowed in this message, at most one per message
      ### 💡 <О чём решаем>         — per `QUESTION_RULE_SLIM` (full format with worked examples lives in
      `QUESTION_FORMAT`, in the interview / vision directives)
      ### ↓ Детали — по желанию    — reasoning, full comparison, change-list (per `AX_PROGRESSIVE_DISCLOSURE`)

      Glyph dictionary — closed inventory, one assigned meaning each, never a free pick. Every glyph
      here is chosen to read clearly on BOTH a light and a dark terminal/chat theme — half-tone shading
      characters (`░ ▒ ▓` and similar) are forbidden anywhere in this layout: they render as near-invisible
      or vanish outright depending on theme.

      Section-header glyphs (fixed, one per header, in the order above):
      - `🤔` — the agent's own understanding check, at the top of a decision card
      - `🎯` — the crux decision, in plain words
      - `💡` — a decision the agent is proposing for the operator to confirm or pick between
      - `↓` — folded detail, expand on demand

      Step-TYPE glyphs (fixed, keyed by the step's TYPE, used in the service line / breadcrumb, never a free pick):
      - `🏗` — creation / scaffold (new spec, new tickets, new files)
      - `🔍` — audit / review (fresh-eyes read, no write)
      - `🔧` — fix / reconcile (spec ⟷ code drift repair)
      - `⚡` — execute (a task ticket's phases running)
      - `🗺` — routing / overview (intent classification, project-level map)

      Breadcrumb-status glyphs (per `BREADCRUMB_FORMAT`): `✅` done · `👷` active · `◻️` not yet.

      No other emoji appear in message or section headers — the glyphs enumerated above are the only
      ones this layout permits.
    </Contract>

    <Contract id="BREADCRUMB_FORMAT">
      One line, its own paragraph below the service line — a blank line separates the two (per
      `MESSAGE_LAYOUT`); a single `\n` with no blank line is a contract defect, markdown renders it
      fused onto the service line as one run-on. This session's milestones, each rendered `<Name>
      <status>`, with a status marker chosen for legibility on BOTH light and dark themes — no
      half-tone shading characters (`░ ▒ ▓`) anywhere, they vanish depending on theme. Status set: `✅`
      done · `👷` active (the step running now) · `◻️` not yet reached. Delta only; never re-list
      everything already settled. This is the «where are we», and it replaces a verbose run-on of
      finished steps.

      `Vision ✅ · Scope Graph 👷 · Infra ◻️ · Portal ◻️`
    </Contract>

    <Axiom id="AX_PROGRESSIVE_DISCLOSURE" cross-cutting="true">
      Decision first, reasoning on demand. The must-read top of a message is short: where we are + my
      read + what to decide. Everything heavy — full option comparison, evidence, the change-list,
      derivations — goes BELOW a `### ↓ Детали — по желанию` header. Never dump reasoning above the
      questions. Facts already verified collapse to one line («сверился: …»); uncertainties that need
      the operator BECOME the questions — never list them twice.
    </Axiom>
  </ChatOutput>

